[Desktop Entry]
# HACK: overrides the package's launcher entry (same file id in
# ~/.local/share/applications wins over /usr/share/applications). It is a copy
# of /usr/share/applications/omnigent-desktop-electron.desktop with one flag
# added to Exec. Because it shadows the package file entirely, any upstream
# change to Exec/Icon/MimeType is masked: re-diff against the package entry on
# every bump of OMNIGENT_DESKTOP_APP_VERSION in desktop-app.env.
#
# Bug: on a fresh machine (no window_bounds in ~/.config/Omnigent/settings.json)
# the GUI dies with SIGTRAP within a second, silently. Electron centers the
# window when it has no saved position, and on a fractionally scaled sway
# output Chromium's Wayland fractional-scale path then requests an empty
# xdg-shell window geometry, which trips CHECK(!bounds.IsEmpty()) in
# ui::XdgSurface::SetWindowGeometry (ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/xdg_surface.cc).
# Once any run has saved bounds the centering path is skipped and the crash
# never recurs, which is why it only bites first launches. Observed 2026-09-07
# with Omnigent 0.10.0 / Electron 42.7.0 / Chromium 148.0.7778.280 on sway
# 1.11 at output scale 1.2. VS Code, Cursor (Electron 42.10) and Chrome 152
# do not hit it with fresh profiles: they pass an explicit window position.
#
# Fix: --disable-features=WaylandFractionalScaleV1 keeps the app on native
# Wayland with integer buffer scaling (compositor downsamples). Verified the
# only other working variant is --ozone-platform=x11 (blurrier);
# --force-device-scale-factor=1 and WaylandPerSurfaceScale still crash.
#
# Remove this file (and its link in sync.sh) once the app no longer needs it:
# either Omnigent ships explicit window bounds / this flag itself, or its
# pinned Electron carries a Chromium where the CHECK path is fixed. To test,
# delete "window_bounds" from settings.json and run the package Exec with
# core dumps off:  (ulimit -c 0; /opt/Omnigent/omnigent-desktop-electron)
# A window means the hack is obsolete; "Trace/breakpoint trap" means keep it.
Name=Omnigent
Exec=/opt/Omnigent/omnigent-desktop-electron --disable-features=WaylandFractionalScaleV1 %U
Terminal=false
Type=Application
Icon=omnigent-desktop-electron
StartupWMClass=Omnigent
Comment=Omnigent desktop shell (Electron edition) — a thin native wrapper around the server-served web UI.
MimeType=x-scheme-handler/omnigent;
Categories=Development;
